body:
Thanks for the report, @RanadeepPolavarapu! Easy repro in the [demo](http://eslint.org/demo):

``` js
/* eslint max-len: ["error", 16, { "ignoreComments": true, "ignoreTemplateLiterals": true }] */

const a = `asdffdsaasdffdsaasdffdsa
asdffdsaasdffdsaasdffdsa
asdffdsaasdffdsaasdffdsa
asdffdsaasdffdsaasdffdsa`;
```

This gives a `max-len` error on the second and third lines of the literal. It looks like [`groupByLineNumber`](https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/c85fd84d627dc2788197b9cba26cb843dbe57d8d/lib/rules/max-len.js#L237-L241) is only handling the first and last lines of the literal and not any interior lines.

@RanadeepPolavarapu do you want to put together a pull request to fix this?
